<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">British North Borneo Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1881">1881</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as North Borneo Chartered Company</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">North Borneo</a> Company was a chartered company that governed North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>, modern Sabah, from 1881 to 1946 under a British royal charter. It held lands acquired from the sultans of Brunei and Sulu, ruled through a governor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sandakan">Sandakan</a> and developed tobacco and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> estates. It also administered Labuan from 1890 to 1906. After the Japanese occupation it ceded North Borneo to the British crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-north-borneo-company.jpg" alt="British North Borneo Company" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: North Borneo Chartered Company · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BNBCC-Logo_(after_1930).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
